--  WHAT THIS IS
--    A Nape extender + titan auto-farm + gas refill + results-screen retry,
--    driven entirely through the Vega UI in vega_ui.lua. It is written for the
--    Delta Android executor: real Instances for the menu (no Drawing), and the
--    proven client-side movement from the earlier AOTR recon in this repo.
--
--  v3.0 ADDS (all optional, all off unless noted)
--    Round automation : auto start missions / raids / waves / mastery,
--                       raid type rotation, hardest available difficulty,
--                       modifier clicking, boss-skin rejoin, solo mode.
--    Movement         : tween travel (default, anti-cheat friendly), hover and
--                       teleport modes, stuck detector, auto rejoin.
--    Combat           : cluster targeting for group hits, auto skills, auto
--                       escape, infinite spear ammo, auto reload.
--    Progression      : skill-tree unlocker, perk equip / enhance / sell,
--                       slot select, prestige, boosts, crates, achievements.
--    Family           : roll / store with a Mythical webhook.
--    Webhooks         : rewards, mission completions, lifetime stats.
--    Visuals          : 3D rendering off, performance mode, fog removal,
--                       auto-hide menu.
--    Safety           : shadow-ban heuristic, stuck fail-safe, auto-execute.
--
--  GAME-UI AUTOMATION AND WHAT IT MEANS
--    AOTR's menus are not part of the measured recon below, so every button is
--    found by NAME OR TEXT with a broad alias list, inside the panel named by
--    the matching word (Raids, Modifiers, Perks...). If this game build renames
--    a button, that one action reports "button not found" and nothing else
--    breaks. Tools -> Dump UI prints every visible button and label so one
--    rename can be handled in seconds (edit the alias lists in GuiAuto).
--
--  HOW TO RUN (Delta, Android)
--    0. Easiest: paste aotr_delta_bundle.lua on its own. It is this same build
--       with Vega embedded, so it needs no second file, readfile or loadstring.
--    1. Two-file route: put vega_ui.lua and aotr_delta_farm.lua in Delta's file
--       workspace (Files -> Import, both files, same folder).
--    2. Execute aotr_delta_farm.lua. It reads vega_ui.lua from the same folder.
--       If that lookup fails, run vega_ui.lua first and then this script: it
--       reuses getgenv().Vega.
--    3. The menu opens on its own. Tap Start farming (or press F5). During a
--       run the menu collapses to a 46px title bar at the top-left: tap its "-"
--       to reopen it, then Stop. F5 still stops from a keyboard.
--
--  WHAT WAS MEASURED IN THIS GAME (not assumed)
--    * workspace.Titans holds the models. Each has HumanoidRootPart and
--      Hitboxes.Hit.Nape. The nape is a plain Part welded to the titan.
--    * Nape .Size writes stick. Nape .Position is reverted by the weld within a
--      frame, so the magnet re-asserts it EVERY frame; most frames it holds.
--    * Our own HumanoidRootPart accepts .Position / .CFrame, so hovering is a
--      repeated write plus zeroed AssemblyLinearVelocity.
--    * A nape hit DELETES the titan. Humanoid health therefore never shows the
--      kill, so kills are counted from the player's own Stat attribute.
--    * The farm loop that produced 4 kills in 6 seconds was exactly: hover
--      above the titan, pull the nape onto the player, aim, mouse1click.
--    * Gas: Unclimbable.Camps.Camp.GasTanks.Refill is the camp tank. R only
--      refills while the character is standing on it. Gas percentage is read
--      from PlayerGui.Interface.HUD.Main.Top...Gas.Percentage.
--    * Blades: Rig_<player>.LeftHand/RightHand.Blade_1..7, Transparency == 1
--      means broken.
--    * Results: Interface.Rewards.Main.Info.State reads COMPLETED / FAILED.
--      Rewards buttons are in the order Leave_2, Modify, Retry, so the game's
--      own key navigation is backslash, D, D, Enter. This build fires the
--      Retry button through getconnections first and only falls back to keys.
--
--  WHAT THIS DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO
--    * No hookfunction / metamethod hooks. Every update to this game moves
--      client code, and a hook is the first thing that breaks. The executor
--      functions that ARE used are optional and probed one by one:
--      getconnections + firesignal + isexecutorclosure (fire the real Retry
--      button, skipping our own connection), fireproximityprompt and
--      firetouchinterest (refill without a keyboard), mouse1click /
--      mouse1press + mouse1release (attack), keypress + keyrelease (R), and
--      setrobloxinput when present. Missing ones fall back or disable exactly
--      one path; the menu and farm keep working.
--    * No remote / teleport spam. Titans are server-owned; the farm moves YOU.
--    * No auto-leave. If a round cannot be retried, the status line says so.
--
--  API (from the executor console)
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.start()      start the loops
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.stop()       stop the loops and release input
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.toggle()
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.restore()    put every remembered nape size back
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.retry()      press the results screen Retry now
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.selftest()   print PASS / FAIL / INFO for every path
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.status()     one-line state
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.cfg          live table; edit any field while it runs
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.stats        lifetime counters (saved to Vega/aotr_stats.json)
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.rejoin()     teleport back into the place
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.dumpUI()     print every visible button / label
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.installAutoExec()  write the Delta autoexec loader
--    _G.AOTR_DELTA.destroy()    stop, restore, unload the menu
--
--  SAFETY
--    F5 farm on/off, F6 nape extender, F7 panic (stop + restore + park).
--    Panic and Stop both release mouse buttons and R / Space / W. Stop does
--    not restore nape sizes; Restore napes does. Rejoining does not need a
--    restore: the old parts are gone and the next round starts at stock size.
--============================================================================

